00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:39.940
<b>Rejected</b>

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:39.940
<i>That's what I'd like to know! Why </i>am<i> I here?!</i>

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.120
<i>I'm quietly trying my best 
not to yell at anyone,</i>

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:43.510
<b>Guidance Office</b>

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:43.820
<i>and suddenly I'm being interviewed!</i>

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:47.860
You'll never get into college if you 
can't handle an impromptu interview!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.290
<i>Say what?</i>

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:53.120
You have zero academic ability, 
so you need to practice your interview skills.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.660
<i>That's not true!</i>

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.040
<i>And what's with this suit, anyway?</i>

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.330
<i>Did he prepare this just for me?</i>

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.920
Did you forget, Seri-kun?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:02.400
I'm the treasurer of the student council, 
and thus I control the budget.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:05.180
<i>Hey, don't waste it on things like this.</i>

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.940
What's wrong, Gestöber?

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:09.890
You should have more confidence 
and talk about what makes you special.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:14.830
If you tell them how you're working toward 
world peace as the Hierophant of Ice,

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:17.160
they'll see the good in you, 
no matter how bad you look.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.480
<i>Who looks bad here?!</i>

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.900
<i>Also, I refuse to do that!</i>

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.070
<i>They'd kick me right out!</i>

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.350
Nonsense. There's nothing 
but good in Koyukichi-dono.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:27.360
There's no need to use so many words.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.790
<i>Yeah, the fewer the better
from someone who talks like you.</i>

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.980
You're just spoiling him!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:39.750
<b>GRRR</b>

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:39.750
<b>GRRR</b>

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:39.750
<b>GRRR</b>

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.490
You're not thinking about 
what's really best for Gestöber!

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:37.200
And you're underestimating him, Kabu-dono!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.580
The hell'd you say?

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.750
The hell'd <i>you</i> say?

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.930
Okay, okay. Calm down.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:44.930
The interviewer just saw all of that.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:49.430
The interview begins the 
moment you walk in the door.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.430
<b>Hanadori\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKoyuki\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMogami</b>

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.430
<b>Poop</b>

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.380
<i>Hey, Reaper, what did you just write?</i>

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:54.370
Okay, I have a question for you all.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.220
Can you tell me why you chose our school?

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.280
<i>That's actually a normal question.</i>

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.940
<i>Maybe this will actually be helpful...</i>

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:06.600
It is my destiny to protect this world,

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:10.050
but its people have not 
yet realized it's in danger.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:13.340
I seek an environment 
where I can spread the word,

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:14.910
and this university is ideal.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:17.820
I still have much to learn.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.370
I need someone to beat 
the stupidity out of me,

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:24.250
and I believe the professors at your 
school are just the people for the job.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.900
I see. Thank you.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:29.220
Lastly, let's hear from shorty.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.640
<i>You just called me "shorty" again. I heard that.</i>

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.680
Well?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:37.800
I've dreamed of being a teacher ever 
since I was in elementary school,

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:41.500
s-so I want to study at your school's
 education department.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:43.320
I see.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.260
So what made you want to be a teacher?

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.070
Huh? Um, well...

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.990
My cousin was a teacher, 
and I wanted to be like him.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.460
And what about him did 
you find so engaging?

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.100
U-Um...

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.710
<i>Why do I keep getting the hard questions?</i>

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.660
<i>These two are way worse than me.</i>

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:08.010
<b>Hanadori\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKoyuki\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMogami</b>

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:08.010
<b>God\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPoop\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMask</b>

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:04.160
I see.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:08.020
So you don't have any kind of clear 
ideas about being a teacher.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.100
And you think you can get into our 
education department like that?

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.220
<b>GRRR</b>

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.220
<i>Damn it. He's laughing at me.</i>

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:18.640
Next, please tell us about any kind of
 special talents or hobbies you might have.

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.600
<i>Special talents or hobbies?</i>

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:27.000
I play homemade Japanese stringed instruments
while repenting my failure as a human being.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.660
<i>You do that much repenting? 
Forgive yourself already.</i>

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:32.620
<i>What should I say?</i>

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.550
<i>I've got nothing, really.</i>

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.320
<i>I'm not in any clubs...</i>

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.580
Gestöber, you know what to say!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.480
You know, the Stealthy Ninja Blizzardwalk!

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.800
<i>I haven't heard that one in a while!</i>

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:47.500
<i>I still have no idea what 
kind of skill it even is.</i>

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:50.190
<i>I know you're trying to help, 
in your own annoying way, but...</i>

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.720
<b>Hanadori\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKoyuki\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMogami</b>

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.720
<b>God\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPoop\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMask</b>

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.720
<b>God\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPoop\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h</b>

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.790
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.900
<i>I don't have anything good to say.</i>

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:58.680
<i>Teaching really is my dream, though.</i>

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:01.310
I need to straighten up a bit.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:05.300
<i>Are these guys going to be 
like this the rest of their lives?</i>

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:08.030
<i>I'm actually a little worried.</i>

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:09.460
Okay, lookin' good!

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.240
<i>I'm jealous that they don't seem worried...</i>

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.780
Do you have anything, Hanadori-kun?

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:15.660
Me?

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.570
Well...

00:16:17.480 --> 00:16:20.200
I do have one thing to show you.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.450
I can do a little Nanjing Lily.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.920
<i>Traditional performance art?!</i>

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.670
<i>Why do you have a talent like that?!</i>

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:29.830
I learned it for shows when I was in my band.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:30.800
<i>No way...</i>

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.260
<i>What the hell kind of band was Dead Bull?</i>

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.830
Looky here, looky here!
Looky, looky, looky here!

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:41.580
Look, it's the Nanjing Lily!

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:45.860
Flip it over, flip it over,

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.760
and it turns into Gestöber!

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:51.030
<i>They love it!</i>

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:52.610
<i>I just...</i>

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:56.200
<b>Mitoya
High School</b>

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.200
felt the wave energy 
of Miguel's Nanjing Lily!

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:57.530
Hey, you there...

00:16:58.600 --> 00:16:59.340
Let me go!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:03.460
Do you know how many years it's been 
since I've seen Miguel's Nanjing Lily?

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.460
Right, right. Knock it off.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:08.870
Let me see it... Miguel's Nanjing Lily...

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.670
You just like saying that, don't you?

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.140
Miguel!

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.350
<i>I think I just heard something...</i>

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.970
Is there anything else?

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:21.930
Well, I can also do a little 
bit of singing, sutra-copying,

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.100
and ballroom dancing.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.390
My interests right now 
are aquariums and kabuki.

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:28.320
<i>You're kidding me.</i>

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.140
<i>That sounds so aristocratic...</i>

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:33.290
I'd love to try horseback riding, 
too, but horses scare me.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.320
<i>Are you an aristocrat?!</i>

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.780
<b>God</b>

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.980
How about tea ceremony 
and calligraphy, Kabu-dono?

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:38.760
<i>That's way too many hobbies!</i>

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.970
<i>Is he really doing all that?</i>

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.080
I'd love to try them.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:44.080
Martial arts are great, too.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:46.400
<i>No, given how much trouble he 
has communicating with others,</i>

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.140
I'd love to learn Japanese drums, myself.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.720
<i>it won't be easy for him to...</i>

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.170
All right, please share any ambitions you 
might have for your time at our school.

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:54.400
<i>Ambitions? Um, um...</i>

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.470
Don't show the interviewer your butt, shorty.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:04.310
I want to use my experiences in high school 
to become a teacher that students can trust,

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:10.280
a-and live a peaceful campus life 
unperturbed by annoying classmates.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.910
<i>I feel terrible saying that.</i>

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.080
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:17.120
<i>I realized I don't have any real ambitions.</i>

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:22.220
<i>At some point, I just fixated on finding a
better place than where I am right now.</i>

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.340
<i>Wait, but...</i>

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:27.120
<i>Maybe I'm lucky to realize my weakness.</i>

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:31.410
<i>Compared to this guy who's never grown 
out of being a dark god of destruction...</i>

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.420
Certainly.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:38.300
In this economy, a certification 
or a degree isn't enough to get by.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:42.930
It really concerns me to see
 so many of my upperclassmen

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:47.440
fall so far into student loan debt that 
they have to live at home to repay it.

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:51.880
They choose whatever job pays the 
most and give up on their dreams,

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:57.180
and in their despair, they tell themselves 
everything is fine and lose their inner child.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:05.660
So I want to set clear goals for myself and 
strive toward them while I'm still in school.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:11.010
Being a "good kid," doing what you're told
 and fitting in, may be what society wants.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:15.980
But it doesn't make you the kind of 
person who can <i>change</i> society,

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:19.010
because you'll never be 
extraordinary that way.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:23.200
Unfortunately, the world 
may not always be at peace.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:30.020
So even if I never really do fit in, 
I hope young people share my concerns.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:36.820
I want to be able to decide for myself 
who I should and shouldn't listen to.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:40.510
And I want to share the way 
I feel with lots of people.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:46.280
I know for a fact that when everyone 
remembers their mission in life,

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.460
they have the power to change the world.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.480
And that the world is always with them.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:56.420
And that someday, they won't be able 
to deny the vibrations of their soul.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:58.580
Remember, sheeple!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.710
You weren't always sheeple!

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:03.280
You aren't in chains at all!

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.710
That's what I to share with people

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:09.460
to wake their hearts from their slumber.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.030
Why are you shining?!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.030
Miguel-senpai!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.030
Koyuki-dono!

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.420
Since when were you so woke?! 
Why are you thinking about all that?!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:20.220
What's wrong? I-I'm sorry, Gestöber!

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.780
Do you enjoy making me worry?!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.640
And halfway through, you totally 
stopped making any sense!

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:24.780
Strong light needs deep darkness
 as its counterpart.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:25.800
Don't worry.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:28.150
Even if you flunk your entrance 
exams or end up unemployed,

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:30.840
or get corrupted and fall to 
the bottom of the social ladder,

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:33.040
I'll be with you!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.050
Damn it all!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:39.300
<b>Hanadori\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKoyuki\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMogami

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:36.330
Worry not, Koyukichi-dono!

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.320
If you're broke, you can always live with me.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:45.550
<b>Hanadori\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKoyuki\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMogami

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:42.640
Miguel-senpai, if I stay by Gestöber-senpai,

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.670
can I shine, too?

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:45.560
What does that even mean, Grim Reaper?!

